+# Audit: large text (0.20.0)
+
+Date: 2026-11-03 · PR: Cochilo 0.22.0 · Auditor: Claude (graphic-design-fundamentals + impeccable)
+
+## Scope
+
+A rule only: `docs/accessibility.md` "Text scaling" now covers min heights for headers and bars,
+flowing chip rows, and the label scale cap (150%) for icon-backed tab labels and chart axis ticks.
+No token values change.
+
+## graphic-design-fundamentals (§13 checklist)
+
+| # | Question | Result |
+|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Brief | Pass: every word readable at the largest system font size |
+| 2 | Concept | Pass: grow, wrap between words, never clip |
+| 3 | Hierarchy | Pass: display and label roles keep their order at 200% |
+| 4 | Contrast | Pass: unchanged |
+| 5 | Alignment and grid | Pass: chart labels keep one column, which widens with them |
+| 6 | Spacing | Pass: flow rows reuse the chip spacing |
+| 7 | Typography | Pass: no word breaks inside a chip; "Naps: 4" keeps its number |
+| 8 | Colour | Pass: unchanged |
+| 9 | Consistency | Pass: one cap, one rule, two named uses |
+| 10 | Simplicity | Pass |
+| 11 | Real-size test | Pass: Cochilo's 200% screenshots, Pixel 5 |
+| 12 | Accessibility and ergonomics | Pass: the cap only where an icon or a spoken summary carries the meaning |
+| 13 | Production | Pass |
+
+## impeccable (audit, native / Android)
+
+| # | Dimension | Score | Key finding |
+|---|---|---|---|
+| 1 | Accessibility | 4 | Large text no longer hides a choice |
+| 2 | Performance | 4 | No cost |
+| 3 | Appearance & theming | 4 | Unchanged |
+| 4 | Platform conformance | 4 | Matches Material's capped navigation labels |
+| 5 | Adaptivity | 3 | Tablet layout still to come |
+| | **Total** | **19/20** | |
diff --git a/docs/accessibility.md b/docs/accessibility.md
index 35ee58a..00d4b03 100644
--- a/docs/accessibility.md
+++ b/docs/accessibility.md
@@ -6,7 +6,12 @@ Target: WCAG 2.1 AA in every theme an app ships. These are checked per screen be
   `tokens.json` `contrast` and checked by `check_tokens.py`. Don't lighten `muted` or `muted-2`.
 - **Not colour alone.** A state has a word or an icon as well as a colour.
 - **Targets.** 48dp minimum, 8dp apart. Small visuals (the 32dp app switch) sit in a 48dp area.
-- **Text scaling.** sp only; buttons use min height, not fixed height, so 200% doesn't clip.
+- **Text scaling.** sp only; buttons, headers and bars use min height, not fixed height, so 200%
+  doesn't clip. Rows of chips flow (wrap between chips, never inside one; a chip's word never
+  breaks). Two kinds of label may stop growing at **150%** (the label scale cap): a word under an
+  icon that carries the same meaning (the tab bar), and a chart's axis ticks (hours, day names),
+  whose band widens with them. Everything else, and every spoken label, grows in full. Each app
+  keeps a 200% screenshot of its main screens.
 - **TalkBack.** Rows announce label + value + state; icon buttons have a description; switch rows
   are one control; charts, rings and gauges have a spoken summary; header status, timers and
   progress chips are live regions.
